## 2. Artifacts and Project State Sources

Four artifacts with orthogonal roles. Each has a single reason to change and
a single authorized writer.

| Artifact | Role | Update cadence | Authorized writer |
|----------|------|----------------|-------------------|
| `CLAUDE.local.md` | Project rules + standards | Static — not modified during execution | User (manual) |
| `.claude/session-state.json` | **Runtime state**: active task + phase, last commit, last verification | Each TDD phase transition | Agent |
| Git (commits + branch) | **Timeline** of changes; commit prefix (see §5) confirms closure type — TDD phase, task, review fix | Each TDD phase closure or review checkpoint (atomic commit) | Agent |
| `planning/claude-plan-tdd.md` | **Contract + documentary record**: tasks with checkboxes | Only when **closing a complete task** (not per phase) | Agent |

### 2.1 Authority order (drift resolution)

Of the four artifacts above, three carry runtime state — state file, git, and
plan. These can contain redundant information about the same transition; when
they diverge, apply this canon order:

```
1. Git is canon of the past      — commits are immutable, the timeline is truth
2. State file is canon of the present — sole source of "now" during execution
3. Plan is canon of the future + record — what remains + what was completed
```

**Operational rule:** if `.claude/session-state.json` reports `phase=green` but
the last commit is `refactor:`, **there is drift** — abort and escalate to the
user. Recovery is manual, not automatic; silent synchronization hides protocol
bugs.

Recovery if the state file is corrupted or lost: regenerate it from the plan
(last `[x]`) + git (last commit), then escalate to the user for confirmation
before continuing.

### 2.2 State file schema

`.claude/session-state.json` — gitignored, minimal JSON:

```json
{
  "plan_path": "planning/claude-plan-tdd.md",
  "current_task_id": "3",
  "current_task_title": "Extract validation into separate fn",
  "current_phase": "green",
  "phase_started_at_commit": "a3f2d1c",
  "last_verification_at": "2026-04-18T16:30:00Z",
  "last_verification_result": "passed"
}
```

Fields:

| Field | Type | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| `plan_path` | string | Path to the approved plan |
| `current_task_id` | string \| null | Id of the active task; `null` when the plan is `done` |
| `current_task_title` | string \| null | Human-readable title of the active task, for diagnostics; `null` when the plan is `done` |
| `current_phase` | `"red"` \| `"green"` \| `"refactor"` \| `"done"` | Active TDD phase or `"done"` if the task closed |
| `phase_started_at_commit` | string | SHA of the commit that closed the previous phase — marks the point from which the current phase starts |
| `last_verification_at` | ISO 8601 string \| null | Timestamp of the last `/verification-before-completion`; `null` before the first phase closure |
| `last_verification_result` | `"passed"` \| `"failed"` \| null | Result of the last verification; `null` before the first phase closure |

Add `.claude/session-state.json` to the project `.gitignore`.

> **Scope:** `.claude/session-state.json` applies **only** to executions under
> an approved plan (autonomous flow). Under manual flow (fallback without plan)
> the state file is not used — the user tracks each phase manually in prompts.

### 2.3 Write protocol

**Applicability:** the protocol in this subsection applies **only** when
`planning/claude-plan-tdd.md` approved (autonomous flow). Under manual flow
(without plan), the state file is not created, read, or updated.

- **Session open** — two cases:
  - **If it exists** — the agent reads the fields and continues from
    `current_task_id` / `current_phase` without modification. Do not overwrite.
  - **If it does not exist** — the agent creates it by reading the plan (first
    task with `[ ]` + Red phase) and the last commit as `phase_started_at_commit`.
    Fields `last_verification_at` and `last_verification_result` are initialized
    to `null` (no phase closure has occurred yet).
- **When closing a phase** — the agent updates `current_phase`,
  `phase_started_at_commit`, and the verification fields inside the state file,
  **after** the atomic commit for the phase (see §5).
- **When closing a complete task** (all 3 phases closed) — the agent marks `[x]`
  on the corresponding checkbox in the plan, commits the plan change with prefix
  `chore: mark task {id} complete`, and updates the state file: advances
  `current_task_id` + `current_task_title` to the next `[ ]` in the plan and
  **resets `current_phase` to `"red"`** (the new task starts in Red).
  If **there is no next `[ ]`** (this was the last task), apply the "When closing
  the plan" protocol below instead.
- **When closing the plan** — all tasks `[x]`; the agent sets
  `current_task_id: null`, `current_task_title: null`, `current_phase: "done"`
  in the state file.

### 2.4 Rules vs state separation

`CLAUDE.local.md` contains **rules** — immutable during execution. Agents
**read and enforce** them; they never modify them. Modifying rules requires
manual user intervention and review of the impact on the active plan.

All ephemeral state (task, phase, progress) lives in the three state artifacts
of §2 (state file, git, plan). Never in `CLAUDE.local.md`.

> **Note on section numbering:** Sections §3 (TDD cycle), §6 (code review),
> and §7 (finalization) are intentionally not in this file — they are
> procedural and live in the `sbtdd` orchestrator skill. Numbering is kept
> aligned with the skill's cross-references.

