## 4. Project Stack

```
Stack:         (filled by /sbtdd-init)
TDD Guard:     tdd-guard (3 hooks via .claude/settings.json, see §4.1)
```

TDD-Guard integrates via PreToolUse/SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit hooks
(full detail in §4.1 below). No external reporter required; enforcement is
real-time on each Write/Edit.

### 4.1 TDD-Guard hook configuration

Three hooks in the project's `.claude/settings.json`:

| # | Hook | Matcher | Command | Role |
|---|------|---------|---------|------|
| 1 | `PreToolUse` | `Write\|Edit\|MultiEdit\|TodoWrite` | `tdd-guard` | Validates that the cycle is not violated before executing the write |
| 2 | `SessionStart` | `startup\|resume\|clear` | `tdd-guard` | Initializes TDD-Guard state on session start or resume |
| 3 | `UserPromptSubmit` | *(no matcher)* | `tdd-guard` | Enables quick commands `tdd-guard on` / `tdd-guard off` |

#### Full `.claude/settings.json` content

```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit|TodoWrite",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "tdd-guard" }]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "tdd-guard" }]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "tdd-guard" }]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Save to `.claude/settings.json` (developer-local configuration —
see tracking policy in §1; `.claude/` is entirely gitignored, each developer
instantiates their own hooks).

#### Verify the 3 hooks are active

```bash
cat .claude/settings.json | jq '.hooks'
# Must show: PreToolUse, SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit
```

